{# Executive summary and coverage statement - B-2 (Milestone 2, section 8.3).

   One page, straight after the cover: the summary, then the coverage
   statement below it. Each renders only when its switch is on
   (sections.executive_summary, sections.coverage_statement) and B-2 returned
   text; with only one of them, that one renders alone under its own heading.
   The next section starts on a new page, as every section does.

   Each text sits in a framed block with the brand rule down its left side; the
   summary's first paragraph, the run's verdict, reads as its lead. Lists print
   as striped tables (_narrative.html.j2).

   The text is B-2's verified output, every figure in it filled from the record
   or its derived values; nothing here adds to it. Autoescaped. #}
{% from "_narrative.html.j2" import blocks %}
<section class="section executive-summary" id="executive-summary">

  {% if executive_summary %}
    <h2>Executive summary</h2>
    <div class="narrative summary-narrative">
      {{ blocks(executive_summary, "summary-points") }}
    </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if coverage_statement %}
    {% if executive_summary %}
      <h3 class="narrative-head">Coverage statement</h3>
    {% else %}
      <h2>Coverage statement</h2>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="narrative coverage-narrative">
      {{ blocks(coverage_statement, "coverage-points") }}
    </div>
  {% endif %}

</section>
